# Accepted trivy findings (Android SBOM scan and production image scan in
# scripts/ci/dependency-audit.sh), same contract as
# accepted-vulnerabilities.txt: one CVE/GHSA id per line, with a comment
# explaining why it cannot be fixed yet and what the way out is. Everything
# not listed here fails the audit at HIGH/CRITICAL.

# --- pip's vendored dependencies ------------------------------------------
# All three live in pip's own vendor tree, not in anything this repository
# installs: /usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip/_vendor/bom.cdx.json is
# a CycloneDX SBOM that pip ships to describe what it bundles, and trivy reads
# it. A stock python:3.14-slim reports them before a single line of our
# Dockerfiles has run, and pip 26.2.2 is the current release -- there is no
# version of pip to upgrade to that vendors newer copies, and pinning our own
# setuptools/msgpack does not touch pip's tree.
#
# Way out: drop these three lines when a pip release refreshes its vendored
# msgpack to 1.2.3 or later and setuptools past 78.1.1, and confirm with
#   trivy image python:3.14-slim --scanners vuln --severity HIGH,CRITICAL
CVE-2025-47273   # setuptools 70.3.0, PackageIndex path traversal. pip vendors
                 # pkg_resources, not the easy_install PackageIndex the
                 # advisory is about.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  # msgpack 1.1.2, out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse.
                     # pip uses it through cachecontrol, on responses from the
                     # package index it is already trusting for code.
CVE-2026-114613  # msgpack 1.1.2, memory leak (denial of service). Same copy,
                 # same path: pip 26.2.2, the current release, still vendors
                 # 1.1.2. Our own msgpack in /opt/venv is 1.2.3.

# pip 26.2.1 vendors urllib3 2.7.0 (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt), next to the 2.8.0
# our requirements install in /opt/venv. Same shape as the two above: trivy
# reads pip's own vendor list, and there is no pip release to upgrade to.
# pip only runs while an image is built, against PyPI, without a proxy; no
# service calls pip at runtime, so neither path below is reachable in
# production. The urllib3 our code imports (safe_fetch.py, requests) is 2.8.0.
#
# Way out: drop these two lines when a pip release vendors urllib3 2.8.0 or
# later (check pip/_vendor/vendor.txt), then rebuild the images.
CVE-2026-97687   # urllib3 2.7.0, HTTPS proxy TLS configuration override.
                 # pip's image builds use no proxy.
CVE-2026-97689   # urllib3 2.7.0, unbounded memory in the chunked-response
                 # parser. Only PyPI responses reach it, at build time.
